{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301810-scion-2e-still-buggy-char-creation-broken","id":1301810,"title":"[Scion 2e] Still buggy? Char Creation Broken","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-01T22:04:41-07:00","id":1301810,"title":"[Scion 2e] Still buggy? Char Creation Broken","content":"So I'm a little confused here. There still seems to be some mistakes in both scion books dealing with character creation... specifically concerning upgrading from an origin character to a hero character?<br /> <br /> 1. Knacks: the book says &quot;Choose additional Knacks, as described in Step 5. If your pre-Visitation Scion already knows more than five Knacks, add four additional Knacks from their Callings&quot; <br /> <br /> This seems to imply that if your origin character has less than 5 knacks then they don't get the extra 4 at hero..<br /> <br /> Step 5 says &quot;For each Calling, choose a number of Heroic Knacks equal to the Calling\u2019s rating; while they can learn more, they may only have as many active as they have Calling dots. Alternately, you may choose a single Immortal Knack instead of two Heroic Knacks for any Calling two dots or higher&quot;<br /> <br /> So... there's a bit of confusion there as to what to do here...<br /> <br /> 2. Birthrights: the book says &quot;Assign seven dots worth of Birthrights if you haven\u2019t already, as described in Step 6. If you\u2019ve spent some, spend the rest&quot;<br /> <br /> Meanwhile step 6 says &quot;Your character receives seven dots to allocate to Birthrights&quot;<br /> <br /> Having said that... origin states that a character can get 4 points of birthrights if they forgo the knacks.<br /> <br /> Does this mean a character can keep those or do they only get an extra 3 at the cost of the extra knacks in origin? Which further implies they get punished for not choosing the extra knacks st origin for not having 5 or above?<br /> <br /> The wording is confusing. Having said that... with the wording... &quot;If you\u2019ve spent some, spend the rest&quot; implies that because there is no other reference to buying boons aside from origin... then you only get 3 extra dots if you chose that option in origin... but step 6 implies that you just allocate an extra 7 regardless. <br /> <br /> Anyone? Devs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/488-blackwood","name":"Blackwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar488_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T22:47:30-07:00","id":1301813,"title":"","content":"As I see, the visitation put everybody in the same level, 5 knacks and 7 birthrights. If you had 4 and 1 you get 1 and 6.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a little word, it sounds a little like \u201cwhatever you did, nothing matters\u201d, but it\u2019s what it sounds like...<br /> <br /> The knack thing is another thing, if you have more than what you can use, just keep an stock you can exchange after each scene. This is another thing that put everybody more or less in the same step all the time, as the only way to increase calling is screaming Legend and it needs a group working togheter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T23:11:41-07:00","id":1301814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301810-scion-2e-still-buggy-char-creation-broken?p=1301813#post1301813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I see, the visitation put everybody in the same level, 5 knacks and 7 birthrights. If you had 4 and 1 you get 1 and 6.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a little word, it sounds a little like \u201cwhatever you did, nothing matters\u201d, but it\u2019s what it sounds like...<br /> <br /> The knack thing is another thing, if you have more than what you can use, just keep an stock you can exchange after each scene. This is another thing that put everybody more or less in the same step all the time, as the only way to increase calling is screaming Legend and it needs a group working togheter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get that's the intention but as worded.. it doesn't remotely sound that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/488-blackwood","name":"Blackwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar488_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T23:26:56-07:00","id":1301815,"title":"","content":"Yeah... there appear to be a number of things in the recent PDF release that are sort of sloppy. This is just one of them. The Legend/Boons table is still... probably wrong, unless the intent was changed, the pregens are still something of a mess, Creatures do now have health suggestions but no defenses, among other issues. I'd suggest going with intent if you can make it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","user":"HighPriest","date":". 04-02-2019, 02:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T23:40:37-07:00","id":1301818,"title":"","content":"I'm just hoping to hear something concrete from Neall. It's his baby after all. The issue is with most things in the book. There is not enough explanation or clarity or even examples. I find a lot of the stuff is either contradictory or doesn't explain how it works with other rulings","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/488-blackwood","name":"Blackwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar488_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T00:41:19-07:00","id":1301822,"title":"","content":"The Kami pantheon skills don't match between the two books, origin has culture persuasion and Hero has culture close combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2472-trebius","name":"trebius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2472_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T02:35:29-07:00","id":1301835,"title":"","content":"Hey y'all, reporting in. Neall made a comment on the Scion Discord, it's possible that the files uploaded are older versions on accident. He's going to double-check everything when he can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T04:32:36-07:00","id":1301857,"title":"","content":"Yeah, just to echo this, I want to double-check everything when I can, but let me emphasize that I don't know what was going on or uploaded, so please don't say &quot;it's possible they were older files&quot;. If necessary I'll issue errata to reconcile the two, but some errors are bound to happen.<br /> <br /> It's worth noting that some clarifications simply didn't make it in for space, and character creation is one of them. No, if your Origin character doesn't have more than five, you don't get an extra four. Origin characters should start with one; Hero characters start with five. The additional dots are for converting characters; if your Origin character has been played for a few sessions and the player bought Knacks, you don't get a bunch of free ones because you made the leap to Hero.<br /> <br /> The Birthright wording is because of the necessity of Purview access meaning you've likely pre-spent some of your Birthrights for your concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T06:43:36-07:00","id":1301887,"title":"","content":"Im going to try and hold any frustrations but I really hope you are not saying that if a mistake was made and if the wrong pdf was sent off to the printer with tons of unerrataed changes that were reported that we the fans, have to accept that, and use a issued errata sheet with our printed books. If the wrong file was used for printing, that really needs to be addressed at the expense of Onyx Path to make sure they are reprinted using the proper changes that were supposed to be there. I don't think fans will be willing to accept a &quot;oops&quot; with the final version especially with how much silence there was at the end and how this final version was never showed to any fans despite the fact we clearly showed we could find any changes that still needed made. From the sounds of it, this errata sheet will end up being fairly hefty and will make the entire Scion 2E line look sloppy if its required from day 1. I really hope this gets resolved in a way that is respectful to the fans. The best outcome would be the find out the wrong file simply got uploaded to drivethru.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 04-02-2019, 10:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}